   "publicReleaseNotes": "**Public subscription choices now match the channels your Lamp can send through.** Email remains available, and SMS, Slack and Teams appear when configured. The Teams form links to instructions for creating a Workflows webhook before asking for its URL, and channel result pages offer a way back to subscriptions.\n\n- **Reopening an incident starts from the component state readers last saw.** Its preview and publication no longer use the incident's old, resolved component attachments as the previous state.\n- **Availability report downloads use readable component names.** CSV and PDF filenames use short, file-safe names, with numeric suffixes when names collide.\n- **The subscriber directory names selected components.** CSV invitation batches show their import time and remaining count. On a local Lamp, invitation feedback says no email was sent and links to Confirm locally in the Delivery log.\n- **Managed mail reports who handles sender authentication.** A configured Run Edit Run relay reports that the platform manages authentication, without claiming inbox delivery. An incomplete managed mail connection gives guidance for restoring it instead of asking for a direct-provider credential.\n- **Settings shows the built Lamp version.** The health response also includes `buildVersion` and a version 1 `schemaObservation` with the observed migration count and inventory digest, or a reason the inventory could not be read. This observation is separate from the installation's liveness result.\n\nUpgrading from 1.11.14: back up data and your source changes first, update the checkout to `v1.11.15`, run `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile` and `rer deploy` with the same environment and input file. This version adds no migrations. The checkout keeps rer 0.2.108. Earlier installations also follow the retained upgrade notes below, including keeping `INSTALLATION_KEY` with their private secrets.",
   "contractChanges": {},
   "extensionPointChanges": [],
-  "migrations": [],
+  "migrations": [
+    {
+      "id": "0079_subscriber_directory_order.sql",
+      "buyerSteps": "Apply after 0078 through the ordinary migration runner before starting the updated Worker. Adds the subscriber directory order index; existing subscriber records, consent and delivery history remain unchanged. No account or credential is required."
+    }
+  ],
   "breaking": false,
   "agentUpdateInstructions": "From v1.11.14: back up data and owner source first, update the checkout to v1.11.15, run pnpm install --frozen-lockfile (the checkout keeps @runeditrun/rer 0.2.108) and rer deploy with the same environment and input file. This version adds no migrations. Earlier installations first honor the retained release-history records through 1.11.14, including INSTALLATION_KEY provisioning and backup custody. Preserve all published release records, immutable contract snapshots and applied migration history. Preserve the optional LAMP_PAGE_HOST_ROUTE_ZONE and LAMP_PAGE_HOST_TARGET settings (set together, never with LAMP_HOSTING=workers-dev) and every deploy writing page_settings.hostname equal to LAMP_PAGE_HOST. Run the existing verifier and release validator before adopting."
 }
